# text = Hale had had her vanities as a girl ; had perhaps unduly felt their mortification when she became a poor clergyman's wife ;-- they had been smothered and kept down ; but they were not extinct ; and she liked to think of seeing Margaret dressed for a party , and discussed what she should wear , with an unsettled anxiety that amused Margaret , who had been more accustomed to society in her one in Harley Street than her mother in five and twenty years of Helstone said Mrs .
