# text = Before that Wednesday -- that mournful Wednesday , when Mr . Hale was to be interred , far away from either of the homes he had known in life , and far away from the wife who lay lonely among strangers ( and this last was Margaret's great trouble , for she thought that if she had not given way to that overwhelming stupor during the first sad days , she could have arranged things otherwise )-- before that Wednesday , Margaret received a letter from Mr . Bell Margaret took up a pen and scrawled with trembling hand In her weak state she could not think of any other words , and yet she was vexed to use these .
