# text = Margaret , as if she read his thought , addressed herself to Mr . Bell , both including him in the conversation , and implying that he was perfectly aware of the endeavours that had been made to clear Frederick exclaimed Mr . Bell in surprise said Margaret , a little dismayed said Mr . Lennox , with a little professional dryness of implied reproach interrupting himself rather abruptly said Margaret , softly But he did not say the name ; and although Margaret would have given much to know if her suspicions were right , and it had been Mr . Thornton who had made the enquiry , she could not ask the question of Mr . Bell , much as she longed to do so .
