# text = By dint of questioning , Margaret extracted from her the horrible fact that Betty Barnes , having been induced by a gypsy fortune-teller to lend the latter her husband's Sunday clothes , on promise of having them faithfully returned on the Saturday night before Goodman Barnes should have missed them , became alarmed by their non-appearance , and her consequent dread of her husband's anger , and as , according to one of the savage country superstitions , the cries of a cat , in the agonies of being boiled or roasted alive , compelled ( as it were ) the powers of darkness to fulfil the wishes of the executioner , resort had been had to the charm .
