# text = Bell to reply , looking round , meanwhile , for her old acquaintances Poor Margaret , whose visit was sentimental , not in any degree inspective , felt herself taken in ; but as in some way bringing her in contact with little eager faces , once well-known , and who had received the solemn rite of baptism from her father , she sate down , half losing herself in tracing out the changing features of the girls , and holding Susan's hand for a minute or two , unobserved by all , while the first class sought for their books , and the Vicar's lady went as near as a lady could towards holding Mr .
