# text = There was altogether a tone of forced cheerfulness in the letter , as Margaret noticed afterwards ; but at the time her attention was taken up by Edith's exclamations Margaret drew herself up haughtily Edith began to sob so bitterly , and to declare so vehemently that Margaret had lost all love for her , and no longer looked upon her as a friend , that Margaret came to think that she had expressed too harsh an opinion for the relief of her own wounded pride , and ended by being Edith's slave for the rest of the day ; while that little lady , overcome by wounded feeling , lay like a victim on the sofa , heaving occasionally a profound sigh , till at last she fell asleep .
