# text = Shaw was as good-tempered as could be ; and Edith had inherited this charming domestic quality ; Margaret herself had probably the worst temper of the three , for her quick perceptions , and over-lively imagination made her hasty , and her early isolation from sympathy had made her proud ; but she had an indescribable childlike sweetness of heart , which made her manners , even in her rarely wilful moods , irresistible of old ; and now , chastened even by what the world called her good fortune , she charmed her reluctant aunt into acquiescence with her will .
